{
  "intro": [
    {
      "text": "The land of eastern Roshar once ruled by the Silver Kingdom of Natanatan, now largely unexplored wilderness.",
      "revealedIn": [
        {
          "all": [
            { "book": "way-of-kings", "chapter": "45" },
            { "book": "oathbringer", "chapter": "96" }
          ]
        }
      ]
    }
  ],
  "description": [
    {
      "text": "As a Silver Kingdom, Natanatan covered the southeast corner of the continent, bordering Alethela to the north and Thalath to the west. Its capital, Stormseat, held an Oathgate.",
      "revealedIn": [{ "book": "words-of-radiance", "chapter": "83" }]
    },
    {
      "text": "Highstorms hit eastern Roshar especially hard, and the Natans learned to live with them, farming with crops that grow low to the ground.",
      "revealedIn": [
        {
          "all": [
            { "book": "way-of-kings", "chapter": "58" },
            { "book": "words-of-radiance", "chapter": "55" },
            { "book": "oathbringer", "chapter": "i-1" }
          ]
        }
      ],
      "fromCulture": "food"
    },
    {
      "text": "Natans have pale blue skin, broad noses and white hair with a woolly texture.",
      "revealedIn": [
        {
          "all": [
            { "book": "way-of-kings", "chapter": "36" },
            { "book": "oathbringer", "chapter": "67" }
          ]
        }
      ],
      "fromCulture": "people"
    },
    {
      "text": "Natans treat Roshar's moons as gods and honour the blue moon Nomon most of all. In a folk tale Hoid tells, Nomon fathered a child by Tsa, a queen of the Natans, and her blue-skinned descendants were blessed with grace and beauty.",
      "revealedIn": [
        {
          "all": [
            { "book": "way-of-kings", "chapter": "36" },
            { "book": "oathbringer", "chapter": "67" }
          ]
        }
      ],
      "fromCulture": "religion"
    },
    {
      "text": "People called Natanatan the Granite Kingdom. In Hoid's tale it is a land of rich culture and fine buildings; how much of that is true is unclear, but stories of a civilised Natanatan are still told on Roshar.",
      "revealedIn": [
        {
          "all": [
            { "book": "way-of-kings", "chapter": "58" },
            { "book": "oathbringer", "chapter": "67" }
          ]
        }
      ],
      "fromCulture": "arts"
    },
    {
      "text": "Its old lands now include the Unclaimed Hills, the Shattered Plains, Alethkar's Eastern Crownlands and the eastern Frostlands. People think of the region as an empty wasteland of forests and jungles.",
      "revealedIn": [
        {
          "all": [
            { "book": "way-of-kings", "chapter": "45" },
            { "book": "words-of-radiance", "chapter": "i-4" },
            { "book": "oathbringer", "chapter": "105" }
          ]
        }
      ]
    }
  ],
